      "evidence_type": "published tag insertion in the same loop or domain",
      "functional_impact_measured": "Anti-HA immunofluorescence staining of surface-immobilised virions confirmed robust surface display of the HA tag on SERINC2-containing virions; SERINC2 iHA showed higher staining intensity than SERINC5 iHA. No explicit HIV-restriction or other functional assay reported for the tagged construct.",
      "confidence": "high",
      "rationale": "L1 directly reports an HA epitope-tag knock-in into ECL4 of full-length, membrane-anchored SERINC2, satisfying the insertion-in-this-protein criterion. ECL4 spans residues 290\u2013317 per the authoritative topology landmarks (28 residues, ample room for a ~15\u201323 aa tag). No residue within ECL4 is named in L1 or L2, so insert_after_residue is left null and the site is classified at region level. L2 independently confirms the tag is surface-accessible on virions, supporting surface_only validation. Full-length SERINC2 iHA construct with HA tag inserted into extracellular loop 4 (ECL4, topology landmarks 290\u2013317), expressed in cells and incorporated into HIV virions; surface accessibility confirmed by anti-HA Alexa Fluor 568 staining of surface-immobilised virions (L2). No specific residue within ECL4 is named in either clip.",
      "sources": [
        {
          "pmid": 38785977,
          "citation": "PMID 38785977",
          "claim": "To ensure robust incorporation of SER5 and SER2 into the virions, we performed immunofluorescence (IF) measurements by utilizing the HA tag inserted into the extracellular loop 4 of SER5 and SER2 (referred to as iHA), as previously described [ 24 ]."
        }
      ],
